sage and a `code` such as `INVALID_ID`."},"106":{"id":"/docs/cli-104","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#inspect","content":"Option"},"107":{"id":"/docs/cli-105","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#inspect","content":"Description"},"108":{"id":"/docs/cli-106","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#inspect","content":"`--type`"},"109":{"id":"/docs/cli-107","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#inspect","content":"ID type: `uuid`, `ulid`, `typeid`, `nanoid`, `cuid`, `ksuid`, `objectid`, `xid`, `tsid` (auto-detected if omitted)"},"110":{"id":"/docs/cli-108","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#inspect","content":"`--json`"},"111":{"id":"/docs/cli-109","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#inspect","content":"Output as JSON"},"112":{"id":"/docs/cli-110","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"Check whether an ID is well-formed, one at a time or in bulk from stdin."},"113":{"id":"/docs/cli-111","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"Option"},"114":{"id":"/docs/cli-112","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"Description"},"115":{"id":"/docs/cli-113","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"`--type`"},"116":{"id":"/docs/cli-114","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"Expected ID type (auto-detected if omitted)"},"117":{"id":"/docs/cli-115","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"`--stdin`"},"118":{"id":"/docs/cli-116","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"Read IDs from stdin (one per line)"},"119":{"id":"/docs/cli-117","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"`--quiet`"},"120":{"id":"/docs/cli-118","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"No output, exit code only (`0` valid, `2` invalid)"},"121":{"id":"/docs/cli-119","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"`--json`"},"122":{"id":"/docs/cli-120","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"Output as JSON"},"123":{"id":"/docs/cli-121","page_id":"/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cli#validate","content":"Use `--json` whenever the output feeds another program. The CLI and library publish independently: a library `1.0.0` release does not imply a CLI `1.0.0` release at the same time."},"124":{"id":"/docs/getting-started","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"page","content":"Getting started","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started"},"125":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started","content":"Install eleven type-safe ID strategies, then import only the generator your application needs."},"126":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#install","content":"Install"},"127":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"The usual shape"},"128":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Every strategy"},"129":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#why-byte-helpers-exist","content":"Why byte helpers exist"},"130":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started#write-into-a-caller-owned-buffer","content":"Write into a caller-owned buffer"},"131":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#install","content":"uniku is ESM-only. Import the exact generator you want rather than a package-root barrel:"},"132":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#install","content":"For a Deno project without a package import map, use Deno's npm specifier directly:"},"133":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"The named generator import has two roles. Call it to generate an ID. Use the same value as a dictionary of methods and constants for that strategy."},"134":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"If you are used to class APIs, the attached helpers resemble \"static methods.\" The generator is still a function, so there is nothing to instantiate:"},"135":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"You do not import `toBytes()` or `timestamp()` separately. They stay attached to `uuidv7` and grouped with that strategy."},"136":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"Every generator value exposes `isValid()`. The remaining API matches the strategy. Time-ordered formats expose `timestamp()`. Formats with a canonical binary representation expose `toBytes()` and `fromBytes()`. CUID v2 and Nanoid expose a smaller API because they have no canonical byte representation. UUID v5 is the one generator that takes an input: it derives the same ID from the same name and namespace, and adds `namespace()` plus the RFC 9562 namespace constants."},"137":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"Each generator reference lists the exact call signatures, methods, constants, and overloads available from its imported value."},"138":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Each format is independently importable and tree-shakeable. Install one package, then ship only the strategy your application imports."},"139":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Strategy"},"140":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Direct import"},"141":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Usual function call"},"142":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Primary value"},"143":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"UUID v4"},"144":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"`uniku/uuid/v4`"},"145":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"`uuidv4()`"},"146":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"`string`"},"147":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-22","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[]