ut does not have the format's canonical length."],[558,"A counter option is outside the format's supported bit width."],[622,"A destination buffer offset or range cannot contain the encoded ID."],[195,"A good default"],[703,"A malformed namespace string throws a `ParseError` with code `INVALID_LENGTH`, `INVALID_FORMAT`, or `INVALID_CHAR`."],[704,"A namespace `Uint8Array` that is not exactly 16 bytes throws an `InvalidInputError` with code `BYTES_INVALID_LENGTH`."],[598,"A Nanoid alphabet contains a duplicate character."],[594,"A Nanoid alphabet contains a non-printable ASCII character."],[590,"A Nanoid alphabet has fewer than 2 or more than 256 characters."],[586,"A Nanoid or CUID v2 output length is outside its supported range."],[642,"A parsed or supplied value exceeds the format's numeric range."],[326,"a regression must exceed `max(configured threshold, 2 × combined dispersion)`\nbefore it is reported, and reference-side rows never gate a change;"],[223,"A sortable 64-bit integer, not a UUID-shaped string."],[19,"A standalone binary (no Node.js required) is also available for macOS and Linux:"],[694,"A string name is encoded as UTF-8 and hashed as is. uniku does not apply Unicode normalization, which matches other implementations. `'é'` written as one code point (NFC) and as `e` plus a combining accent (NFD) gives two different IDs. If your inputs can arrive in either form, normalize them first:"],[667,"A string that is not a UUID throws a `ParseError` with code `INVALID_LENGTH`, `INVALID_FORMAT`, or `INVALID_CHAR`."],[695,"A string with a lone surrogate is not valid Unicode. UTF-8 encoding replaces each one with U+FFFD, so `'a\\uD800b'` and `'a\\uFFFDb'` give the same ID. The `uuid` package throws for these strings instead. If your names can contain arbitrary UTF-16, check them first with `String.prototype.isWellFormed()` where your runtime supports it."],[550,"A timestamp option is not an integer in the format's range, or a decoded timestamp overflows."],[614,